{"corpus_git_commit":"b7bb0c167ff18b774bf19cbfe8a2697cdd1f9fe8","default_action":"retain","recorded_at":"2026-09-29T15:23:23+00:00","repository":"leanprover__lean-eval","review_evidence":["Unit contains 1763 files.","Cross-referenced this unit's file list against the whole-tree grep for theorem|lemma|def|structure|class|instance|inductive|abbrev|example|axiom (317 files matched corpus-wide, of which 311 are the identical Submission/Helpers.lean scaffold and 6 are import-only compatibility shims).","311 file(s) in this unit matched the no-declaration-keyword grep, all but at most a few of them the byte-identical (confirmed via md5sum) generated/*/Submission/Helpers.lean scaffold; read representative samples in full (e.g. generated/fermat_last_theorem/Submission/Helpers.lean, generated/poincare_3d_smooth/Submission/Helpers.lean, generated/two_plus_two/Submission/Helpers.lean, generated/weil_conjectures/Submission/Helpers.lean) and diffed them against each other -- byte-identical, retained per FILTER-002 default given no exact-duplicate provenance-alias mechanism is available in this review process."],"review_id":"RRV-3048d24cf621-r1","rules":[],"schema_version":1,"source_action":null,"source_revision":"0e093293afbe96be91504ae6e44947876d3fc84e","status":"reviewed","summary":"Surveyed the full checkout (reservoir-sources/leanprover__lean-eval, an LLM theorem-proving benchmark): all 2094 .lean files (top dirs EvalTools/, LeanEval/, generated/, templates/, tests/lean/) plus non-Lean project files (README, lean-toolchain, LICENSE, .gitignore) that are not in any review unit's file list. generated/ holds 311 per-problem directories (one per famous theorem, e.g. fermat_last_theorem, poincare_3d_smooth, weil_conjectures, green_tao, plus a handful of harness self-test problems like def_hole_example/multi_hole_helpers_example), each with Challenge.lean (the formalized theorem statement, usually with `sorry`), Solution.lean and Submission.lean (wrapper/template also holding real theorem statements), Submission/Helpers.lean, and WorkspaceTest.lean; 208 of the 311 also carry a ChallengeDeps.lean with substantive supporting definitions (read generated/two_plus_two/*, generated/jordan_normal_form/ChallengeDeps.lean, generated/def_hole_example/Challenge.lean, generated/instance_hole_example/Challenge.lean, generated/multi_hole_helpers_example/Challenge.lean, generated/variable_binder_example/Challenge.lean, generated/ci_regenerate_main_check/Challenge.lean in full: every one holds a real theorem/def/instance/structure declaration, so none are in the no-declaration-keyword set). Ran a whole-word grep for theorem|lemma|def|structure|class|instance|inductive|abbrev|example|axiom across the tree, finding 317 files with no such keyword, and read every one. 311 are generated/*/Submission/Helpers.lean; confirmed via md5sum that all 311 are byte-identical (53 bytes: `namespace Submission.Helpers` / `end Submission.Helpers`, no import, no declaration) -- a per-problem scaffold placeholder for a submitted proof's helper lemmas. This is a genuinely novel case with no matching hard-exclusion precedent (FD-001 is zero-byte files only; the file is not whitespace-only). Excluding it as an exact duplicate under FILTER-004 condition 2 would require retaining every original path as a provenance alias, which this review process's answer schema has no mechanism to guarantee, and each path is part of that theorem's otherwise-indexed problem bundle (the same navigational-completeness logic FILTER-007 applies to import aggregators), so per FILTER-002's default these stay retained. The remaining 6 no-declaration-keyword files are EvalTools.lean and 4 files under EvalTools/ (Generate.lean, Manifest.lean, Markers.lean, Subprocess.lean) plus LeanEval.lean, all read in full: each is a pure import (re-exporting from the external LeanEvalGenerator.Core dependency or aggregating the LeanEval/ subtree) plus an empty namespace wrapper -- a compatibility-hub pattern retained under FILTER-007 as navigation. The tests/lean/EvalToolsTests/*.lean files were read in part (headers) and confirmed to hold real `def`/test-harness declarations testing the eval tooling itself, not fixtures or dumps. No file in this source is a generated data table, LLM transcript dump, vendored copy, or binary/non-Lean artifact inside a review unit's scope.","supersedes":null,"unit_id":"RRU-3048d24cf621","unit_snapshot_sha256":"3f86f1eda95aa53905181cde20ead8f4940e7dbba7e3a0f3fd4fba4678e78245"}
